"""Along RL training, step 100 lands near Base + cue at T 1.0 (+1.4 points, 4 samples); most of RL's gain comes later.

The page of one finding, served at /finding/rl-learns-the-opening-first (view.py serves every tools/finding_<slug>.py)
and reached from its tile on /findings, which ICON draws. The picture is one lit plate. On its left, the 500 MATH-500
problems as one mark each, in three bands by the outcome of the one stored answer (finished right, finished wrong, cut
off), blue when the answer opens with 'Okay'. On its right, the count of right answers and a trace of three counts along
training (right answers, 'Okay' openings, cut-offs), with Base + cue as a reference point and a dashed level. At T 1.0
the large number and the row of right answers are four-sample means with the 4 samples as faint ticks (Base: one
sample); the marks, bands and other rows are the one stored answer per problem. The main
control steps through training (Base, step 100, step 400, step 2,800) or shows Base + cue; a second, quiet switch picks
the temperature (T 1.0, the default, or T 0.6); the marks travel to their new bands, the counts and the trace move.
A click on a mark shows that problem's answers at every step and at both temperatures in the side column.
Address: /finding/rl-learns-the-opening-first#<state>/<t0.6>/<panel or p<problem>>, state base, cue, s100 (the
default, left out), s400 or s2800; t0.6 only when T 0.6 is chosen. The rules are in .claude/skills/finding-page/SKILL.md;
the looks are those of tools/architecture.py (.claude/skills/site-ui/SKILL.md).

T 0.6: board item result-32b7a8 and its comment; the round is studies/theory/results/engine/round-04/
(studies/theory/README.md, "Round 04"). Its per-problem rows are not in git: they are the five row files in
runs/replication/ that the round's replication fetched from S3 (studies/theory/results/engine/round-04/replication/
common.py). PROBLEMS is copied from them; the check compares the counts with the committed outputs of the round
(replication/capcounts.out, replication_turn2.json, metrics_v5.json) and of the grader (results/rln4/grader_v3).

T 1.0: board item result-fad48d; studies/rlneurons/README.md, "Released RL checkpoints at T 1.0, plain and cue
(ckptcue)". Every T 1.0 count is computed from committed per-problem rows: results/ckptcue/<cell>-01/per_problem.json
(steps 100 and 400, plain and cue), results/rln4/t1_t3_items-01 (Base and Base + cue) and t1_t2_items-01 (step 2,800).
PROBLEMS1 is copied from those rows; three raw files in runs/ckptcue/ (not in git) add only the first characters of the
step 100, step 400 and step 2,800 answers and step 2,800's extracted answer: the two job answers.jsonl files named in
DATA["t10"]["raw"] (in runs/<job id>/ of the worktree iterate-hack-ckpt) and T2.jsonl (s3 path and sha256 in
results/rln4/grader_v3/readout.json, which the check compares).

    PYTHONPATH=. uv run --no-project --with numpy --with sympy --with math-verify==0.9.0 \
        python tools/finding_rl_learns_the_opening_first.py           checks DATA, PROBLEMS and PROBLEMS1 (needs runs/)
    ... python tools/finding_rl_learns_the_opening_first.py --write   rewrites PROBLEMS and PROBLEMS1 from the rows
"""
